<!--
  CLASSIFICATION FIXTURE. Do not "fix" the TransferCharacteristics value below,
  and note that despite the file name nothing about this profile is invalid.

  A three-component matrix-based RGB Display profile at version 4.5.0.0,
  carrying a HAGC tone-mapping descriptor and a cicpTag that declares
  TransferCharacteristics 13 (IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB). Clause 8.10.1 admits only
  8 (Linear), 16 (PQ) and 18 (HLG), so this profile is NOT of the clause 8.10
  HDR Profile sub-class.

  That is the whole point of the fixture. Clause 8.10.1's conditions are
  definitional - they say which profiles are HDR Profiles, not what a profile
  must do - so missing one is not a violation. This is a perfectly valid ICC
  Display profile that happens to carry a cicpTag and a HAGC tag, both of which
  are legal optional tags of its class. It pins the rule that neither
  CIccProfile::Validate() nor the PAWG report may report anything against it.

  (The HAGC tag is what makes the profile HDR-RELATED enough for the PAWG report
  to open its HDR section at all and state the classification. It is not
  evidence of a defect.)

  Expected: iccFromXml saves the profile; iccDumpProfile -v reports the profile
  as valid; iccPawgReport prints H1 as N/A and no other H item.
  See Testing/expected-invalid-fromxml.tsv.
-->
